<title>GERMANY: German inland gasoil steady, sellers competitive.</title>
<headline>German inland gasoil steady, sellers competitive.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7006)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     34.40/34.60     20.24/20.35   34.40/34.60</p>
<p> BREMEN		34.40/34.60     20.24/20.35   34.40/34.60</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    34.30/34.50     20.18/20.29   34.00/34.50</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   35.10/35.40     20.65/20.82   35.00/35.20</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   35.10/35.30     20.65/20.76   35.00/35.20</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  36.00/36.20     21.17/21.29   36.00/36.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were mostly unchanged on Friday after attempts by distributors to raise prices by 20 to 30 pfennings in the morning were thwarted by aggressive competition amongst sellers.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
